EN-US;mso-bidi-language:AR-SA&quot;&gt;The development, due to the intensification of
the site and the number of people proposed to be on site, would result in an
unreasonable degree of impacts with regard to traffic and parking impacts; and
that the applicant has failed to demonstrate that adequate provisions has been
made for waste, servicing and deliveries, would be contrary to Policies T4.F
and T7.G of The London Plan (2021) and Policies DM42.F, DM43.C, DM44 and DM45 &amp;nbsp;of the Harrow Development Management Policies
Local Plan (2013).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p class=&quot;MsoNormal&quot; style=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:12.0pt;
line-height:107%;font-family:&amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;,sans-serif;mso-fareast-font-family:&amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;;
mso-bidi-font-family:&amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;&quot;&gt;The development, due to the
intensification of the site and the number of people proposed to be on site,
would result in an unreasonable degree of impacts with regard to noise and
disturbance to the detriment of the amenities of neighbouring occupiers,
contrary to Policies D3.D(7), D13 and D14 of The London Plan (2021) and
Policies DM1, DM33 and DM46 of the Harrow Development Management Policies Local
Plan (2013).&lt;b&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p class=&quot;MsoListParagraph&quot; style=&quot;text-indent:-18.0pt;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:12.0pt;line-height:115%;
font-family:&amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;,sans-serif;mso-fareast-font-family:&amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;;
mso-bidi-font-family:&amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;The development, due to the maximum
number of children it could accommodate in conjunction with the amount of floorspace
designated for the childcare use, its poor accessibility and lack of supporting
evidence for the need, would result in an over intensification of the site in
an inappropriate location and a non-residential use on site which, due to its
scale, would no longer be ancillary to the C3 dwellinghouse. The proposal would
therefore fail to comply with Policies H8 and S3.B of the London Plan (2021) and
Policies DM33.A, DM33.E and DM46.B of the Harrow Development Management
Policies Local Plan (2013).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;MsoNormal&quot; style=&quot;margin-left:18.0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:12.0pt;
